      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hello Devoury,\n\n  I've taken a look at a few of the avatars in your account which appear to exhibit this issue.  The problem is that the avatars appear to have multiple VRCPhysBone components enabled at the same time, all which have isAnimated enabled and affecting the same bones.  This is not a supported setup.\n\nPhysbones components prior to the update ran all at the same time, so although the above setup wasn't correct, the results appeared fine.  Now that Physbones run in order, the components affecting the same bones are affecting each other.  One component moves the bones, the next component affecting the same bones sees this as animation, etc.\n\nThis unfortunately is something you will need to fix on your avatars.  Ideally you should never have two physbone components affecting the same bones.  If you do, then those components will need to have isAnimated disabled.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
